        "start_line": 768,
        "end_line": 770,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Double free of mp_name when cpool was allocated before the error",
        "explanation": "pcfg.name is set to mp_name, and mlx5_hws_cnt_pool_init copies pcfg into cpool->cfg, so cpool->cfg.name == mp_name. mlx5_hws_cnt_pool_destroy (line 798) already calls mlx5_free(cpool->cfg.name). On any error after the pool is created (action_create, dcs_alloc or raw_data_alloc fails), destroy frees mp_name and then the new mlx5_free(mp_name) frees it again, corrupting the heap. The original leak only exists when cpool == NULL (svc_init fails or pool_init fails), and the new line fixes only that case.",
        "suggestion": "Free the name only when the pool doesn't own it: `if (cpool == NULL) mlx5_free(mp_name);` before or instead of the unconditional free. Alternatively, set mp_name = NULL right after cpool is created successfully.",
        "evidence": "\tmlx5_free(mp_name);",
